<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bhagadatta</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bhagadatta is a legendary king of Pragjyotisha, the ancient name of Kamarupa in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assam">Assam</a>, son of the demon king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narakasura">Naraka</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahabharata">Mahabharata</a> he is a mighty warrior who rides the elephant Supratika and fights for the Kauravas at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kurukshetra">Kurukshetra</a>, where he is slain by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arjuna">Arjuna</a>. The kings of Kamarupa, including the Varman and later dynasties, claimed descent from Naraka and Bhagadatta.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bhagadatta.jpg" alt="Bhagadatta" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bhoomi · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhagadatta_fighting_with_Bhima.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
